WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.330
<b>Info-Live: The Millione Show</b>

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.470
<i>It's Info-Live: The Millione Show!</i>

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:07.800
<i>Hello!</i>

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.870
<i>Today, we have two guests 
who represent the new era!</i>

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:15.040
<i>There will be Gelsadra-kun, 
an alien from outer space</i>

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:19.020
<b>Alien 
Gelsadra</b>

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:19.020
<b>Gatchaman 
Misudachi Tsubasa</b>

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.870
<i>and Misudachi Tsubasa-chan, 
a new Gatchaman.</i>

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.550
<i>Just look at those youthful smiles.</i>

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:21.000
What's this?

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.090
I wasn't told of this!

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.860
Hey, Hajime!

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.420
Tsubasa-chan's so cute.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.340
Listen to me!

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.130
Please show us!

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.810
So this is the much talked about...

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.560
This is everyone's feelings.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:48.330
They seem to be calling 
you Bubble-sama on-line.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:51.610
Of course it'd be an alien who could 
make that sort of thing happen!

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.510
Well, how is it, anyway?

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:55.220
How is Earth to you?

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:57.530
I'm kind of... disappointed.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.480
Oh? Why's that?

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.740
I'd heard that Earth was blue... 
but everyone...

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:07.420
...doesn't have a blue face!

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:09.840
Your face is too red!

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:16.490
Oh, it's too funny!

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.890
It's an alien joke.

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:20.400
Nice!

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.200
It's not an American joke, 
but an alien joke!

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.680
Good, good!

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:27.920
Whew.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.560
I would've been so embarrassed 
if it hadn't gone over well.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:31.900
My face would've turned bright red!

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.060
It already is!

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.340
You must've practiced this.

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.060
You could tell?

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:41.240
Whew!

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:42.740
Huh?

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.000
Here it comes!

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:55.510
<b>The city 
of teeming masses
is colored crimson 
with determination.
A great wind will save 
the flame of life.</b>

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.920
The city with the teeming masses

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.370
is colored crimson with determination.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:55.900
A great wind will save the flame of life.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:57.280
Crimson...

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.010
So red, huh.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:37.520
So this is the Gatchaman base!

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:38.570
Yep!

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:40.860
Tsubasa-chan!

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.210
Oh, Senpai!

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:44.740
Hey, newbie!

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.490
What was that TV appearance about?!

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.450
Oh, well, that's... uh...

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:51.360
Oh, are you talking about The Millione Show?

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:54.120
Then don't blame Tsubasa-chan.

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:58.450
Millio-chan begged her, didn't he?

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.510
Oh, excuse me.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:05.170
I have another offer from Millio-san.

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:07.510
What?!

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:09.310
<b>Tsubasa-chan! 
 Please come to The Millione Show live next week, too! 
 Oh, and bring Sadra-kun with you, of course!</b>

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:11.430
They've both got it.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:12.970
Got what?

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:14.680
Numbers, man. Numbers.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.680
They're a hot item right now.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:17.940
Let's make them semi-regulars.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.610
You're not a TV celebrity!

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.990
You're one of the Gatchaman, 
protectors of this planet!

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.280
Um, if I may,

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:30.040
I think there are people who'll 
be encouraged if they see a hero!

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.080
We're here!

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.610
And we can protect them in times of need!

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:40.050
I think it's also a hero's responsibility 
to reassure people like that!

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:41.660
Don't you agree?

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:43.810
You don't hold back, do you?

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:45.130
Leader!

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:46.720
"Leader"?!

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:48.230
Hey, Hajime!

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:49.540
She's a good girl!

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:50.900
I know!

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:52.290
Um, Leader.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:53.680
What, newbie?

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.190
What's going to happen to Gel-chan?

00:04:56.450 --> 00:04:57.690
Don't worry.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.980
The protection and observation 
of extraterrestrial life forms

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:01.290
are some of our duties.

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:03.690
We will not cause her discomfort.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.570
Now that we've brought it up,

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:10.140
why don't we let Tsubasa-chan handle 
Sadra-kun's observation and care?

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:10.840
Sure!

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:11.870
You can count on me!

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:17.030
Allow me to introduce myself again.

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:21.210
I am Misudachi Tsubasa, a first-year 
in Nagaoka City Tokiwa High School.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:24.040
I still have a lot to learn, 
but I'm honored to be here!

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.470
I'm Gelsadra.

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:29.760
You already know me, Hajime, 
OD, and Utsutsu, right?

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:30.800
Yes!

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:33.750
Utsutsu-senpai, nice to meet you again!

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.630
I'm gloomy...

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:37.770
Those three, you're meeting 
for the first time.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.290
First, that's Hibiki Jou.

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:42.000
Hi, Miss.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.900
That's Tachibana Sugane.

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:45.670
Nice to meet you, Tsubasa-chan.

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:47.360
Nice to meet you, too.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:51.410
And last but not least, this is Ninomiya 
Rui, who joined right before you.

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:54.330
You're much girlier than me!

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:55.120
Nice to meet you.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.230
That'll be all!

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:58.360
Oh, there's one more person.

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:00.130
You don't need to introduce him!

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.040
Here's the upstart!

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.080
I wants a story where the 
innocent country bumpkin

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.420
gets corrupted by the city!

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.980
Wh-Where's that voice coming from?

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:10.180
It's Katze-san.

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:11.960
Berg-Katze?

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:14.030
Oh, you know him, Gel-chan?

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:14.820
Yeah.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:17.120
He's very famous.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:22.200
You're such a simpleton, Geruru!

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.250
"This is everyone's feelings"—

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:25.950
You're dreamin—

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:28.610
Katze-san's in me.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:30.250
I see.

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:31.820
I don't really get it...

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:34.490
but pleased to meet you all!

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:38.570
Why don't we use this opportunity 
to throw a welcome party?

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:41.480
Oh, but I guess Tsubasa-chan can't drink yet.

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:44.630
Sugane, now's not the time for that!

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:47.260
Sorry, Jou-san!

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:50.100
Are you going to ignore JJ's prophecy?

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:54.790
Are you talking about this?

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:59.500
<b>The city 
of teeming masses
is colored crimson 
with determination.
A great wind will save 
the flame of life.</b>

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:55.660
Indeed.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:59.520
JJ's words guide our actions.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.150
The "flame of life"?

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:02.350
A "great wind"?

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:05.990
JJ is way too vague, as usual.

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:08.480
Crimson refers to red, right?

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:10.490
I have some ideas about that.

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:11.620
If we're talking red...

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:13.290
we're talking about CROWDS.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:16.530
VAPE, the organization 
controlling the red CROWDS.

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:19.040
During their previous attack on Nagaoka,

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.250
a man identifying himself as their 
leader showed up in front of Rui.

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:25.110
Yes, he said to me

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:28.400
that they were violent pacifists...

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:31.070
Violent... pacifists...

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:32.860
How interesting!

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:34.550
Now's not the time to be 
finding them interesting.

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:37.660
Why would pacifists 
do such horrible things?

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:41.190
To wipe CROWDS out from the world.

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:44.540
They're intentionally 
causing havoc with CROWDS

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:47.860
so that people would realize 
the threat CROWDS pose.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:52.070
Huh? But isn't it just the red 
CROWDS who are dangerous?

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:53.700
Not necessarily.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:58.140
There were some reports of pranks 
and crimes committed by blue CROWDS.

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:01.770
X just took care of them before 
things got too out of hand,

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:03.710
so they never received 
much attention. That's all!

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:05.640
I see.

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:09.270
In the end, humanity wasn't 
ready for the CROWDS ability.

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:10.930
I disagree.

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:15.840
Unfortunately, there are people 
who use CROWDS for crime.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:19.040
But nothing goes well on the first try.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:22.480
We should move forward, 
even if we have to fail several times.

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:24.700
You're welcome to believe in evolution,

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:27.280
but what if society collapses 
before that happens?

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:29.860
It's not like we have 
all the time in the world.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:34.100
I don't think updating the world 
will take that much time.

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:38.490
The VAPE leader is a self-driven 
man in the extreme.

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:41.430
He has taken a wrong turn,

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:43.380
but he's very principled.

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:45.170
If there were more people 
like him who could direct

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:46.450
their energy on the right path...

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:47.960
If there were, huh?

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.420
You're being idealistic.

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:52.170
What's the point of having 
a world without ideals?

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:54.590
What do you think, Miss?

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:55.930
Huh? Me?

00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:01.500
I just want to become a hero 
who can protect everyone.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:03.700
I'll try my best to do that!

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:04.350
Yeah!

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:09.150
The newbie is far more realistic.

00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:16.390
Room 103 will be for the two of you.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:19.400
Okay! Thank you.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.440
You must be tired from the long trip.

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:25.160
Your beds are ready, 
so you should go to sleep early.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:27.610
Rui-senpai, you're really nice!

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:30.370
What's wrong?

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:35.080
Oh, I was just thinking that you and Jou-san

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:36.810
must have a similar sense of justice.

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:38.790
Katze-san?

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:41.680
Hello, Katze-san?

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.340
Silence...

00:09:44.010 --> 00:09:47.480
If the VAPE leader can control CROWDS,

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.370
that means he's had his NOTE extracted,

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:51.410
just like Rui-kun's was, right?

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:52.900
Silence...

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:56.930
The only one I know who can 
do that is you, Katze-san,

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:58.330
but is that true?

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:00.370
Hello, Katze-san?

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:01.450
Katze-san?

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:02.380
Fine!

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:04.610
And here I was enjoying my relaxation!

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:05.650
Fine, fine, fine!

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:08.000
I was the one who extracted Rizumin's NOTE,

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.380
but so what?

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:11.370
You've got a problem with that, dumbass?!

00:10:11.780 --> 00:10:14.760
What kind of person is he? 
The VAPE leader?

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:17.810
Well, you could say he's serious!

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:19.110
Totes serious!

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:23.100
But those types are the worst 
when they snap, ya know?

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:31.650
Well, let's begin, shall we?

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:41.070
This is...

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:46.660
It's VAPE!

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:58.200
<b>[Live Broadcast] Crisis in Shibuya! Red CROWDS Rioting!</b>

00:10:56.410 --> 00:10:58.220
So that's what this is about...

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:00.470
Got it.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:10.480
<b>Urgent News: Panic in Shibuya! 
 Red CROWDS Appear en Masse--City Turns Scarlet!</b>

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:10.480
<b>Shibuya, Tokyo</b>

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.890
Are you seeing this, viewers?!

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:13.230
The entire city of Shibuya is scarlet!

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:16.070
I've never seen such a thing!

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:16.860
What's this?!

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:18.670
Are they hostages?!

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:22.330
Several citizens appear to be 
restrained by the red CROWDS!

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.370
Oh, look! Blue CROWDS!

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:27.360
<b>Don't underestimate us, 
red CROWDS!</b>

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:34.790
It's not working!

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:36.650
They're powerless!

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:41.800
Their organization is 
almost organized military.

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:46.310
The blue CROWDS have no organization. 
They don't stand a chance.

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:49.070
Let's do this!

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:52.290
We Gatchaman are the ones 
who protect the planet!

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:58.900
Go, Bird!

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:06.340
Listen up!

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:08.040
There can be no casualties!

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:09.700
One, two!

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:11.410
Gatcha!

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:16.540
The Gatchaman!

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:18.460
The Gatchaman have come!

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:23.380
Why can't I fight?

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:28.260
But you can't even 
transform at will yet, right?

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:31.180
Wouldn't you just hold everyone back?

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:32.500
Well...

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:38.730
Sonic Demon Blade!

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:40.480
Storm!

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:43.700
Flame Feather!

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:53.100
Fight until this life of mine 
is extinguished, my shards.

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:54.220
Roger.

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:59.380
Bite and Build!

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:02.920
The Right Arm of Death!

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:09.760
Petites Ciseaux!

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:14.690
Blanc et Noir!

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.100
Digitize!

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:30.080
<b>Caller ID Blocked</b>

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:34.840
Hello, Ninomiya Rui-kun.

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:37.250
This is Suzuki Rizumu, isn't it?

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:39.750
Ninomiya Rui, hand over your NOTE.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.130
I can't do that!

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:45.130
I see.

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:47.970
Then people will die.

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:53.330
Until now, we have kept human 
casualties to a minimum.

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:55.970
That will end today.

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:58.740
Are you going to abandon them?

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:02.140
Are you going to avert your gaze 
again from the lives that were lost

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:05.970
and continue to only preach 
the utility of CROWDS?

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:09.660
Just like you did for 
the Tachikawa Incident?

00:14:12.270 --> 00:14:14.700
I'm sure you had noticed,

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:16.400
that in the shadows of your victory,

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:19.280
there were those who fell victim to CROWDS.

00:14:21.740 --> 00:14:23.150
Enjoy your isolation,

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:27.170
Ninomiya Rui-kun, you foolish idealist.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:31.180
Hajime-chan, I'm leaving this to you!

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:33.070
I'll go, too!

00:14:45.850 --> 00:14:48.410
That's Ninomiya Rui-san!

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:50.590
Who's that before him?

00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:52.370
Is he one of the VAPE members?

00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:56.200
Why do you reject CROWDS so much?

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:59.910
Monkeys don't deserve such power.

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:03.840
In time, CROWDS will just 
become a means for violence

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:05.460
for monkeys are easily 
swayed by public opinion.

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:07.060
That's not true!

00:15:07.060 --> 00:15:08.130
People can change!

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:09.970
Two to six to two.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:13.390
Only a handful can change.

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:17.290
You know that in your heart.

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:18.970
No!

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:21.820
I believe each and every 
one of us can evolve!

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:23.280
To update the world, we need—

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:25.850
You should stop with the idealism.

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:29.980
You just don't want to lose CROWDS.

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:34.350
To me, you look like a spoiled child

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:40.000
who doesn't want his 
CROWDS toy taken from him.

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:43.590
Out, Bird.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:47.950
Oh!

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:51.680
Ninomiya Rui-san has transformed back.

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:53.800
What are you trying to pull, Rui?

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:55.830
You may be right in that

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:59.390
I'm fixated on the idea of CROWDS.

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:01.230
But

00:16:01.990 --> 00:16:04.810
I'm holding fast to my hope. 
I want to believe in everyone!

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:09.570
You asked me, too,

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:11.500
if I also believe in you.

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:12.450
Yeah.

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:18.500
I believe in you...

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:22.640
that you are a man who 
is driven by the right principles.

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:36.440
Ninomiya Rui-kun,

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:38.510
you're so...

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:03.330
so... foolish.

00:17:04.300 --> 00:17:05.750
Oh, he collapsed!

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:06.850
Rui-senpai!

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:09.910
Ninomiya Rui-san just collapsed, 
with blood coming out of his mouth!

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:11.750
There's so much blood!

00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:13.650
Someone call the ambulance! Hurry!

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:15.970
I can't stand to watch this!

00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:19.290
What are the other Gatchaman doing?!

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:21.730
Rui-kun, we're coming!

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:22.640
No!

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:23.530
Don't come!

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:26.860
Rui-san's getting up!

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:28.810
Fight! Fight!

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:31.530
This... is my fight.

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:33.770
I'm not going to lose!

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:36.160
I'll believe in him until the very end...

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:38.280
You idiot!

00:17:38.650 --> 00:17:40.370
Now isn't a time for that!

00:17:41.320 --> 00:17:42.650
Go, Jou-san!

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:43.700
I'll hold—

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:46.020
Sugane?!

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:53.100
I won't be what kills you.

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:56.300
It'll be your foolish ideals.

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:03.600
Rui-rui blood-fest, yeah!

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:05.730
Go, Rizumin!

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:08.110
So, so yummy!

00:18:08.110 --> 00:18:10.520
Katze-san, shut up.

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:12.610
<b>Urgent News: Mr. Ninomiya Rui Bleeding! 
 Gatchaman vs. VAPE</b>

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.280
How could he?

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:18.420
He'll pay for this!

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:20.220
No, Tsubasa-chan.

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:22.630
Hold it in.

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:25.110
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:18:25.110 --> 00:18:26.680
<i>This needs to stop!</i>

00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:28.190
<i>Someone!</i>

00:18:29.350 --> 00:18:31.720
<i>Someone do something!</i>

00:18:32.530 --> 00:18:33.960
I'll go!

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:36.830
Wait.

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:40.010
What good are we if we don't go now?

00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:43.390
I thought Gatchaman are 
heroes who protect everyone!

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:44.770
You're right.

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:48.070
It's our mission to protect people's lives.

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:50.240
But Tsubasa-chan,

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:52.990
people have principles 
that can't be sacrificed,

00:18:52.990 --> 00:18:54.560
even if it means losing their lives.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:58.570
Rui-kun's fighting that fight right now.

00:19:00.210 --> 00:19:01.770
Would you still go?

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:03.740
Of course!

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:07.180
I see.

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:10.370
Tsubasa-chan!

00:19:34.220 --> 00:19:35.020
No...

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:36.690
<b>I can't stand this 
Please help him 
Someone do something  
Screw you, VAPE 
Rui-kun's gonna die! 
This is too horrible  
What's the gov't doing?</b>

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:38.690
I don't want this!

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:40.400
Senpai!

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:43.120
Tsubasa-chan, watch out!

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:44.870
Please get out of the way!

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:48.830
Tsubasa-chan!

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:08.970
What the hell?!

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:10.900
Tsubasa-chan!

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:15.180
If we can't help people in need,

00:20:16.780 --> 00:20:20.960
how can we call ourselves heroes?!

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:29.640
Hundred Fireworks!

00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:46.280
Oh, I see now!

00:20:55.930 --> 00:20:57.730
If that's what everyone wants...

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:03.890
we'll become heroes!

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:07.990
Innocent Storm!

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:23.550
Stay away!

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:40.590
Take flight,

00:21:42.390 --> 00:21:44.610
wings of hope!
